            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thx for quick turnaround: that builds now. \n\nI can file this in a separate issue, but: now I hit a failure at runtime with a nogil block with the amended test case below: \n\n#### reproabi3t.pyx\n```py\n# cython: language_level=3\n# cython: freethreading_compatible=True\n\ncdef class Thing:\n    cdef int value\n\n    def __init__(self, int v):\n        self.value = v\n\n    def get(self):\n        return self.value\n\n    def bump(self):\n        with nogil:\n            self.value += 1\n        return self.value\n```\n\n#### setup.py\n```py\nfrom setuptools import Extension, setup\nfrom Cython.Build import cythonize\n\next = Extension(\n    \"reproabi3t\",\n    [\"reproabi3t.pyx\"],\n    define_macros=[\n        (\"CYTHON_USE_MODULE_STATE\", \"1\"),\n        (\"Py_LIMITED_API\", \"0x030f0000\"),\n        (\"Py_TARGET_ABI3T\", \"0x030f0000\"),\n        (\"CYTHON_OPAQUE_OBJECTS\", \"1\"),\n    ],\n    py_limited_api=True,\n    language=\"c++\",\n)\n\nsetup(name=\"reproabi3t\", ext_modules=cythonize([ext], nthreads=0))\n```\n\n#### Execution\n```sh\n uv run --python cpython-3.15.0rc1+freethreaded python -X faulthandler -u -c '\nimport sys, reproabi3t\nprint(\"import :\", \"OK, gil =\", sys._is_gil_enabled())\nt = reproabi3t.Thing(42)\nprint(\"get()  :\", t.get())\nprint(\"bump() :\", t.bump())\n'\n```\n\n#### Error\n> \n> Fatal Python error: PyInterpreterState_Get: no current interpreter\n> Python runtime state: initialized\n> \n> Stack (most recent call first):\n>   File \"<string>\", line 6 in <module>\n> \n> Extension modules: reproabi3t (total: 1)\n> Fatal Python error: Aborted\n> \n> <Cannot show all threads while the GIL is disabled>\n> Stack (most recent call first):\n>   File \"<string>\", line 6 in <module>",
