            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Right - that's more difficult I think.\n\n`self.value` is no longer just `__pyx_v->value` but instead becomes `GetCClassTypeData(__pyx_v_self, 0, (PyTypeObject*)__pyx_ptype_11basiccclass_Thing, __pyx_typeoffset_11basiccclass_Thing, struct __pyx_obj_11basiccclass_Thing*)`\n\nI'd already done a fudge inside `GetCClassTypeData` to make it (mostly) work without the GIL (since it's a Python C API call).\n\nHowever `__pyx_ptype_11basiccclass_Thing` and `__pyx_typeoffset_11basiccclass_Thing` are both looked up in the global state. Currently getting the global state requires the GIL and that is one of the big limitations in the whole `CYTHON_USE_MODULE_STATE` thing that there isn't a good solution for.\n\nI'll re-open this for now because it's clearly a combination that doesn't work. Not sure there's a quick solution though\n\nIn principle https://github.com/cython/cython/pull/7237 should help I think (by sending most module state lookup calls through simpler mechanisms so that they can be done without the GIL). That's an early draft though for comments on the vague idea rather than a working implementation of anything.",
